--TEST--
`prepareRename` inside a cast syntax that does not parse is refused, because a parse error holds no symbol, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
int $n = 3;
int $m = (i<|>nt)$n;
--REQUEST--
prepareRename
--EXPECT--
refused: There is nothing to rename here. Put the cursor on a class, a variable, a method, a property, a constant or an enum case.
